  "description": "How far do players get, and which level stops them?\n\n*The* metric for a level-based puzzle game (SPEC §14): the cliff in the curve tells you which level is killing retention. Every panel here is campaign-only — the daily shares a number line with the campaign, so `mode=\"campaign\"` is on every query and a missing one would silently mix two different boards under one `level_id`.\n\n**What this board cannot tell you** is whether a level is *hard* or *boring*. Both look like a cliff. Take the level id to Difficulty calibration (`sodogku-difficulty`) — a cliff with long clear times and high strikes is hard, a cliff with fast clears is people simply stopping.\n\n**Loki-backed, so nothing here can see past Grafana Cloud's log retention.** Widening the time picker does not widen the answer.\n\n**Delivery is at-least-once.** A record can rarely ship twice (export acknowledged, process died before the buffer delete), so read raw counts as approximate. Panels that count *installs* rather than records are immune to it by construction — a duplicate lands in the same `install_id` series and collapses.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
